  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Electronic configuration of the given species are</p><p>a. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mo>Sm</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>62</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>Xe</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></math> b. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Eu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>63</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>Xe</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mn>7</mn></msup></math></p><p>c. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Yb</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>70</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>Xe</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mn>14</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;d.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ce</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>58</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>Xe</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mn>5</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></math></p><p>On the basis of above electronic configuration, only <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Yb</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>70</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> has no unpaired electrons i.e. has fully-filled orbitals. Thus, it is diamagnetic in nature.</p>",
